<worksheet >
    <title>EIPO-3 Inner Products</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, complete all three problems. 
      Complete part c and one other part to earn a P.</p>
  </introduction>  
   <page>
      <exercise>
        <introduction>
            <p>Let <m>V = \mathbb{R}^2</m> have a weighted inner product defined by <m>\langle u, v \rangle = 2u_1v_1 + 3u_2v_2</m>, where <m>u = (u_1, u_2)</m> and <m>v = (v_1, v_2)</m>.</p>
        </introduction>
        <task workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p>If <m>u = (1, -2)</m> and <m>v = (4, 3)</m>, compute the weighted inner product <m>\langle u, v \rangle</m>.</p>
            </statement>
        </task>
        <task workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p>Calculate the distance <m>d(u, v)</m> between <m>u = (1, -2)</m> and <m>v = (4, 3)</m> under the metric induced by this inner product.</p>
            </statement>
        </task>
        <task workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p>Show that this weighted operation satisfies the linearity axiom <m>\langle ku, v \rangle = k\langle u, v \rangle</m> for any scalar <m>k</m>.</p>
            </statement>
        </task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>